{"w":2400,"h":3209,"lines":[{"h":0.017536948848736245,"w":0.064077669779459653,"c":1,"y":0.042056074489492556,"t":"Test 4","x":0.093203883459784739},{"w":0.31067960103352865,"y":0.090031152554575833,"x":0.093203888765589799,"h":0.020560747663551426,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","c":1},{"y":0.12628498999963012,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","c":1,"x":0.095029740131216248,"w":0.82547927856445302,"h":0.024243247249044808},{"t":"Passage 3 below.","h":0.022640362558335125,"c":1,"y":0.14703769573058045,"w":0.17161622365315754,"x":0.092811314661292818},{"w":0.77686335245768234,"x":0.12418406350963286,"t":"Alfred Wegener: science, exploration and the theory","c":1,"h":0.029054348193967905,"y":0.1884826258681771},{"w":0.28590817769368493,"c":1,"t":"of continental drift","y":0.21754391896721237,"h":0.025837160865094466,"x":0.36870693117619868},{"y":0.25739117651709309,"x":0.42468243805900158,"t":"by Mott T Greene","c":1,"w":0.17196594238281254,"h":0.023685892645814999},{"w":0.13203882853190105,"c":1,"y":0.2906976746774762,"h":0.018895348284474811,"t":"Introduction","x":0.091262139027828704},{"w":0.790291239420573,"c":1,"x":0.093203894795353223,"y":0.32554517183328435,"h":0.02038506124621231,"t":"This is a book about the life and scientific work of Alfred Wegener, whose reputation"},{"y":0.34384765814457796,"t":"today rests with his theory of continental displacements, better known as 'continental","h":0.023927958360713486,"c":1,"x":0.093067736893792885,"w":0.79838261922200526},{"c":1,"h":0.019470314667603739,"x":0.093155976681461541,"y":0.36461279554716264,"t":"drift'. Wegener proposed this theory in 1912 and developed it extensively for nearly","w":0.7826328023274739},{"h":0.024533718025944395,"c":1,"t":"20 years. His book on the subject, The Origin of Continents and Oceans, went through","x":0.093094162934379387,"y":0.38134966595511721,"w":0.81386449178059905},{"t":"four editions and was the focus of an international controversy in his lifetime and for","h":0.023030130736924281,"c":1,"x":0.093082244641499778,"w":0.78861185709635406,"y":0.40010869629647927},{"y":0.42195743459420965,"w":0.26045928955078124,"h":0.018982815371124229,"c":1,"x":0.093058184835440164,"t":"some years after his death."},{"t":"Wegener's basic idea was that many mysteries about the Earth's history could be","y":0.4571588239417812,"x":0.095065261385509525,"h":0.020666247216340472,"w":0.76520329793294273,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.4750043737195988,"w":0.80796366373697914,"t":"solved if one supposed that the continents moved laterally, rather than supposing that","x":0.095048257379213977,"h":0.021215040735737878},{"w":0.78463597615559899,"y":0.494882695738043,"c":1,"x":0.093126157885640451,"h":0.019859732274325803,"t":"they remained fixed in place. Wegener showed in great detail how such continental"},{"h":0.02053223131601678,"y":0.51348695136466904,"t":"movements were plausible and how they worked, using evidence from a large number","w":0.81184249877929704,"c":1,"x":0.095048039181217417},{"x":0.095012787807155524,"c":1,"w":0.79641906738281254,"h":0.024192275287948983,"y":0.53041275860104709,"t":"of sciences including geology, geophysics, paleontology, and climatology. Wegener's"},{"c":1,"t":"idea - that the continents move - is at the heart of the theory that guides Earth sciences","w":0.82930562337239577,"h":0.02045513283797884,"y":0.55033188501387031,"x":0.093120924163670987},{"h":0.021733052856825585,"y":0.56865793263456355,"c":1,"t":"today: namely plate tectonics. Plate tectonics is in many respects quite different from","w":0.79827418009440088,"x":0.093098704787687531},{"h":0.021879931773723493,"y":0.58800533431382496,"c":1,"x":0.095041676181546672,"w":0.81188323974609378,"t":"Wegener's proposal, in the same way that modern evolutionary theory is very different"},{"t":"from the ideas Charles Darwin proposed in the 1850s about biological evolution. Yet","w":0.79247848510742191,"h":0.021985433703271107,"x":0.095028558576375419,"c":1,"y":0.60595804851876367},{"t":"plate tectonics is a descendant of Alfred Wegener's theory of continental drift, in quite","w":0.80205362955729176,"h":0.019602414306450378,"x":0.095085868952451066,"y":0.62576998182121901,"c":1},{"w":0.79442204793294269,"t":"the same way that modern evolutionary theory is a descendant of Darwin's theory of","y":0.64338870036679496,"x":0.095028306804935792,"h":0.02145986349040474,"c":1},{"t":"natural selection.","w":0.16357556660970052,"h":0.017347987047237057,"x":0.096887610251754172,"y":0.66444984797452167,"c":1},{"t":"When I started writing about Wegener's life and work, one of the most intriguing things","x":0.097087375157521763,"h":0.019044772709641555,"y":0.70058139562023203,"w":0.81165049235026032,"c":1},{"h":0.020544286234727926,"c":1,"x":0.096988894905764012,"w":0.79825276692708347,"t":"about him for me was that, although he came up with a theory on continental drift, he","y":0.7192186825975122},{"y":0.73732511193214212,"x":0.096988347393565849,"t":"was not a geologist. He trained as an astronomer and pursued a career in atmospheric","w":0.81766042073567702,"h":0.020583011948059671,"c":1},{"x":0.097040265523648556,"h":0.016368253951503542,"w":0.74766703287760417,"c":1,"t":"physics. When he proposed the theory of continental displacements in 1912, ne","y":0.758526571522807},{"c":1,"x":0.09902915161103408,"t":"was a lecturer in physics and astronomy at the University of Marburg, in southern","y":0.77601246125858381,"w":0.76116500854492186,"h":0.016199376947040545},{"t":"Germany. However, he was not an 'unknown'. In 1906 he had set a world record (with","x":0.096924585814991054,"y":0.7900057316553446,"w":0.80616063435872398,"h":0.02536637018031429,"c":1},{"w":0.79438217163085945,"t":"his brother Kurt) for time aloft in a hot-air balloon: 52 hours. Between 1906 and 1908","x":0.096985506546464914,"y":0.81198313245366371,"h":0.020399439446279866,"c":1},{"t":"he had taken part in a highly publicized and extremely dangerous expedition to the","x":0.09697662298937397,"c":1,"w":0.77691523234049487,"h":0.020652450133706868,"y":0.83093955781100959},{"x":0.09700246010704329,"t":"coast of northeast Greenland. He had also made a name for himself amongst a small","y":0.84969734411650988,"w":0.80600631713867188,"h":0.020462057523638388,"c":1},{"h":0.02070162288867794,"c":1,"t":"circle of meteorologists and atmospheric physicists in Germany as the author of a","w":0.76716171264648425,"y":0.86803722257581117,"x":0.096995474261453954},{"x":0.095040363585376236,"y":0.88692073801181159,"h":0.02262124747873473,"t":"textbook, Thermodynamics of the Atmosphere (1911), and of a number of interesting","w":0.79635264078776047,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.90869137135703881,"t":"scientific papers.","w":0.16379619598388673,"x":0.096785328815508317,"h":0.018406788953739595},{"w":0.025242718060811367,"t":"92","y":0.96075581419142475,"h":0.014534883112922281,"c":1,"x":0.097087378736584615}]}